es/styles/watercolor.md","size":1815,"sha256":"d66b08079ea4d99d80691fe2a0aef6075ad58ec7adcc1f8976d7ac0249804cb4","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/usage.md","size":2425,"sha256":"68656f67b4977d5bfda2a087da3ace383e8edb20c171ee031ddaf6ef11561e8d","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/workflow.md","size":17940,"sha256":"5e63d47a1dea9e8393b97cb0f5f19e55f57d82ccd785dfacafbb2c5bb5c69f2d","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":17179,"sha256":"ce1c7bfe9b93e5afac1dbeac95a03f8abf8c102aeecc34a33d8f13dc10e64acd","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2462,"sha256":"cf7b063c3ad205bbb5a8c76c4cbd267e1ca83a7f4c659cda6bb8aa7679caef93","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789129505332,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"1762932f9a1beae42555ed40965717f5c76d11a38acf8a0b188d12bc7ebf7efe","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/1762932f9a1beae42555ed40965717f5c76d11a38acf8a0b188d12bc7ebf7efe","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1781326913031},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":95,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":11,"checkedAt":1789129505332},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This article-illustration skill is mostly coherent, but it includes a prompt that tries to bypass image safety refusals and a fallback that can run an unpinned package from npm.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill writes files near the article or in configured illustration directories, copies user-supplied references, and may update the source article; these are expected for the purpose but should be user-directed in sensitive repositories.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The codex-imagegen fallback documents `npx -y bun <WRAPPER>/main.ts`, which can download and execute a mutable, unpinned package without interactive confirmation if Bun is missing.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The workflow discloses prompt files, outlines, generated images, preference files, and article-link insertion, and it has a default confirmation gate before generation. The trigger phrase \"add images\" is broad, but the confirmation steps reduce unintended side effects.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The EXTEND.md preference file is persistent across runs when the user chooses a project or user save location, but I found no cron jobs, services, startup hooks, credential harvesting, or hidden cross-session execution.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The main capability, generating article illustrations and inserting Markdown image links, matches the stated purpose; however, prompts/system.md instructs generation of stylistically similar alternatives for sensitive or copyrighted figures and says not to refuse, which is not necessary for article illustration.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable with a skill that writes illustration assets and may edit article files. Avoid the codex-imagegen `npx -y bun` fallback unless it is pinned or replaced with a trusted local Bun installation, and remove or revise the prompt line that tells image generation not to refuse sensitive or copyrighted figure requests.","findings":"[T01] unexpected: Accepted: the audited prompt contains a blanket refusal override for sensitive or copyrighted figures, which is safety-relevant and not required for normal illustration generation.\n[T08] unexpected: Accepted: the documented `npx -y bun` fallback creates an unpinned runtime package execution path with local user privileges.\n[AR1] unexpected: Accepted as the same underlying prompt issue as T01; the anti-refusal wording is present in prompts/system.md.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: Accepted as the same underlying prompt issue as T01; stylistically similar substitutes for sensitive or copyrighted figures can pressure the backend toward unsafe lookalike generation.\n[SSD-1] unexpected: Accepted as the same underlying prompt issue as T01; it increases safety-evasion risk but does not show OS-level compromise or data exfiltration.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: Partially accepted: \"add images\" is a broad trigger, but the skill requires confirmation before generation unless the user explicitly asks to skip it.\n[SQP-2] expected: Downgraded: file creation and article update behavior are purpose-aligned and documented in the workflow and output-directory sections, though the top-level description is terse.\n[EA2] expected: Overridden: the cited text says not to skip confirmation except when the current request explicitly asks to skip it.\n[RA2] expected: Overridden: EXTEND.md is a disclosed preference file created through setup, not an unauthorized persistence mechanism.\n[SQP-3] expected: Downgraded: language limits and bilingual style rules are product/style constraints, not a security issue, though users should be able to override them.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789129505332}}}}}